1
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:15,890
Molly, I need your special talent for handling special matters.

2
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:18,668
Like what special matters?

3
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:21,740
Well, I have a scheduling problem.

4
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:22,038
Yes?

5
00:00:22,038 --> 00:00:26,157
I have three tonsillectomies set for Friday with Dr. Earl.

6
00:00:26,157 --> 00:00:26,491
Yes?

7
00:00:26,491 --> 00:00:30,614
I need to fit a fourth operation into his schedule.

8
00:00:30,614 --> 00:00:33,958
And ... I know you can do it.

9
00:00:33,958 --> 00:00:35,736
Who's the patient?

10
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:36,281
Carl Herrera.

11
00:00:36,281 --> 00:00:37,645
The boy has infected tonsils,

12
00:00:37,645 --> 00:00:42,257
and we should remove them as soon as possible.

13
00:00:42,257 --> 00:00:42,692
Well, I'll try to arrange the schedule, Dr. Stewart.

14
00:00:42,692 --> 00:00:45,669
But it's not going to be easy.

15
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:51,225
I know you'll be able to take care of it.

16
00:00:51,225 --> 00:00:53,025
Well, Mrs. Herrera,

17
00:00:53,025 --> 00:00:56,581
Carl will be perfectly fine after we remove his tonsils.

18
00:00:56,581 --> 00:00:59,559
Thank you for your reassurance, Dr. Stewart.

19
00:00:59,559 --> 00:01:02,537
He's had so many colds and sore throats recently.

20
00:01:02,537 --> 00:01:05,515
Well, it's a very easy operation, Carl.

21
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:06,875
You won't feel a thing.

22
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:08,493
But when do they do it?

23
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,913
This Friday.

24
00:01:10,913 --> 00:01:14,449
But Saturday's my birthday.

25
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:18,537
Well, we could reschedule the operation, Mrs. Herrera,

26
00:01:18,537 --> 00:01:21,565
but I don't want to put it off too long.

27
00:01:21,565 --> 00:01:23,683
No, I think it's important to do it now.

28
00:01:23,683 --> 00:01:26,361
We can have a birthday party for you, Carl,

29
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:27,961
When you come out of the hospital.

30
00:01:27,961 --> 00:01:30,499
But it won't be on my birthday.

31
00:01:30,499 --> 00:01:33,062
But your health is more important, Carl. Believe me.

32
00:01:33,062 --> 00:01:35,925
I don't want my tonsils out.

33
00:01:35,925 --> 00:01:40,776
Nurse Baker, would you come in, please?

34
00:01:40,776 --> 00:01:51,518
Hello, Mrs. Herrera. Hi, Carl, how you doing?

35
00:01:51,518 --> 00:01:53,163
I don't want my tonsils out.

36
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,363
Come with me, Carl.

37
00:01:56,363 --> 00:01:58,797
You and I will talk this over.

38
00:01:58,797 --> 00:02:03,765
She has a special way with kids.

39
00:02:03,765 --> 00:02:05,074
She sure does.

40
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:19,964
Carl, does your throat hurt?

41
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:20,464
Yes.

42
00:02:20,464 --> 00:02:24,039
OK. Do you want to get better?

43
00:02:24,039 --> 00:02:24,405
Yes.

44
00:02:24,405 --> 00:02:27,800
OK. We want you to get better, too.

45
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:29,574
You'll have your tonsils out tomorrow,

46
00:02:29,574 --> 00:02:32,189
and you won't get so many colds anymore.

47
00:02:32,189 --> 00:02:34,316
But if I have my tonsils out tomorrow,

48
00:02:34,316 --> 00:02:37,190
I'll miss my birthday party on Saturday.

49
00:02:37,190 --> 00:02:38,499
I know.

50
00:02:38,499 --> 00:02:41,803
It's a problem, isn't it?

51
00:02:41,803 --> 00:02:44,455
Let me try to work something out.

52
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:45,121
What?

53
00:02:45,121 --> 00:02:48,206
I have to think about it.

54
00:02:48,206 --> 00:02:50,271
You're fooling me.

55
00:02:50,271 --> 00:02:52,014
Oh, I'm not, Carl.

56
00:02:52,014 --> 00:02:54,354
Give me a chance to think about it,

57
00:02:54,354 --> 00:02:56,700
and I'll come up with something.

58
00:02:56,700 --> 00:02:57,700
A surprise?

59
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:58,200
Maybe.

60
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:01,078
But you just put on your pajamas and robe,

61
00:03:01,078 --> 00:03:02,496
and I'll think of a surprise.

62
00:03:02,496 --> 00:03:04,634
Will it hurt?

63
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:04,934
No.

64
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:07,034
There are other boys and girls here,

65
00:03:07,034 --> 00:03:08,750
and they're having their tonsils out.

66
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:09,603
You'll meet them.

67
00:03:09,603 --> 00:03:11,922
I don't want to.

68
00:03:11,922 --> 00:03:14,801
Change your clothes, Carl.

69
00:03:14,801 --> 00:03:17,801
Everything will be just fine.
